{#- The Weekly Thing's gadget (site/js/gadgets/weekly-thing.js): the latest issue and the last 52 weeks of sends, read
    by the reader's browser from the newsletter's JSON Feed. Only what has been sent, never when the next one goes
    out: a send time would be a promise to readers, and that is Jamie's to make. #}
<div class="gadget weekly-gadget" data-weekly-gadget data-feed="https://weekly.thingelstad.com/feed.json" data-ref="{{ 'https://weekly.thingelstad.com/' | ref('gadget') }}" hidden>
  <h3>{{ thing.gadget.title }}</h3>
  <p class="weekly-latest" data-weekly-latest aria-live="polite">Reading the feed.</p>
  <ol class="weekly-weeks" aria-hidden="true">{% for n in range(52) %}<li></li>{% endfor %}</ol>
  <p class="weekly-axis muted" aria-hidden="true"><span>A year ago</span><span>This week</span></p>
  <p class="weekly-count" data-weekly-count></p>
  <p class="muted gadget-note">Your browser reads this once a visit from the <a href="https://weekly.thingelstad.com/feed.json">Weekly Thing’s JSON Feed</a>, which carries every issue. Each mark is a week, Monday to Sunday in Minnesota, filled when an issue went out.</p>
</div>
